DESCRIPTION
  ipaws is a  Fortran library providing the formulas for computing light and heavy water properties.
  The formulas are taken from http://iapws.org. 

FEATURES
- R2-83
    - [x] Tc in H2O and D2O
    - [x] pc in H2O and D2O
    - [x] rhoc in H2O and D2O
- G7-04 
    - [x] kH
    - [x] kD
- R7-97
    - [x] Region 1
    - [ ] Region 2
    - [ ] Region 3
    - [x] Region 4
    - [ ] Region 5
- R11-24:
    - [x] Kw

DOCUMENTATION 
  The API is written as POSIX-style man pages which distributed with 
  the binaries. 
  
  PDF   https://milanskocic.github.io/iapws/man/iapws-bookman.pdf
  HTML  https://milanskocic.github.io/iapws/index.html

INSTALLATION 
  See the install file.

NOTES FOR FORTRAN USERS
  To use iapws within your fpm(1) (https://github.com/fortran-lang/fpm)
  project, add the following lines to your file:

     [dependencies]
     iapws = { git="https://github.com/MilanSkocic/iapws.git" }

